{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Is it a small thing that you have taken my husband?</b> You should not have consented to become my rival wife, as it says: וְאִשָּׁה אֶל אֲחוֹתָהּ לֹא תִקַּח לִצְרוֹר (Leviticus 18:18)." "<b>And you would also take my son's mandrakes.</b> So as to increase his love for you and his hatred for me." "<b>Therefore let him lie with you tonight.</b> So that the action and property of the mandrakes may take effect in you before they take effect in me — and no harm will reach you from what you give me of them now, for they will not cease from being effective for you afterwards; all the more so since they are ownerless, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 72:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:31.236452033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}